WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.413
Policy is next.

2
00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:06.348
Group Policy was Active Directory's most
ambitious delivery system, and its most

3
00:00:06.348 --> 00:00:10.988
network-bound: a client applies it only
when it can reach a domain controller.

4
00:00:10.988 --> 00:00:15.138
A cloud-native endpoint gets its
configuration from the cloud instead.

5
00:00:15.138 --> 00:00:18.881
The replacement is several
surfaces: Intune for devices,

6
00:00:18.881 --> 00:00:23.741
Conditional Access for access control,
and Azure machine configuration,

7
00:00:23.741 --> 00:00:28.362
through Arc, for servers, because
Intune doesn't manage Windows Server.

8
00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:31.388
The program's pattern is
regenerate, not copy.

9
00:00:31.388 --> 00:00:34.215
Porting a fifty-setting
policy as fifty modern

10
00:00:34.215 --> 00:00:37.624
settings carries forward dead
weight and old conflicts.

11
00:00:37.624 --> 00:00:41.713
Microsoft's own recommendation is
to start new rather than migrate.

12
00:00:41.713 --> 00:00:43.987
Four rules govern every change.

13
00:00:43.987 --> 00:00:46.887
Each setting has exactly one owning layer.

14
00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:48.790
Require is preferred to block,

15
00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:53.430
because a bad block locks users out and
a bad require adds a step you can fix;

16
00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:57.006
blocks are kept for cases such
as legacy authentication,

17
00:00:57.006 --> 00:00:59.288
which the federal baseline demands.

18
00:00:59.288 --> 00:01:03.212
Every change passes plan
validation, a simulated tenant,

19
00:01:03.212 --> 00:01:06.301
a report-only pilot, and
only then production.

20
00:01:06.301 --> 00:01:10.875
And the emergency access accounts are
excluded from every blocking policy.

21
00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:16.202
The decision is the CISO's: the control
requirements every surface must meet,

22
00:01:16.202 --> 00:01:20.863
meaning the Conditional Access
baseline, MFA strength and logging.

23
00:01:20.863 --> 00:01:25.151
Gate G1 needs that baseline
enforced, with no user outside

24
00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:29.950
the MFA requirement except the
documented emergency accounts.
